# Supabase Backend Rules

## Migrations
- All schema changes via version-controlled migrations in `supabase/migrations/`.
- Never manage schema through the Supabase dashboard alone.
- One migration per logical change. Name: `YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_descriptive_name.sql`.
- Include RLS policies in the same migration as table creation.

## RLS Mandate
Every table MUST have RLS enabled with appropriate policies before being considered done:
```sql
ALTER TABLE table_name ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
-- Policies for SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE (if needed), DELETE (if needed)
```
- Customer data: users see only their own rows (`auth.uid() = user_id`).
- Staff data: role-based via `staff_roles` lookup table.
- Financial data: restricted to finance/admin roles.
- No table ships with RLS disabled.

## Edge Functions
- Deno/TypeScript in `supabase/functions/`.
- Use for: ContiPay webhook handling, SMS triggers, inventory transfer approvals, demand forecasting.
- Never put business logic only in edge functions — core logic lives in `packages/shared/`.

## Typed Client
- Generate types: `supabase gen types typescript --local > packages/supabase-client/src/database.types.ts`
- Hand-written query helpers in `packages/supabase-client/src/queries/`.
- Never use `any` for database row types.

## Realtime
- GPS delivery tracking: `delivery_locations` table with Realtime enabled.
- Inventory transfer approvals: Realtime subscription for dual-authorization workflow.
- Use `supabase.channel()` with row-level filters, not broad table subscriptions.

## Storage
- Diagram images: `catalog-diagrams` bucket (public read).
- Staff ID cards: `staff-ids` bucket (authenticated read only).
- Payslips: `payslips` bucket (owner read only).
